  'Electronics teaches how semiconductor devices become useful analog circuits. The syllabus links device physics to circuit models, biasing, small-signal analysis, amplifiers, op-amps, frequency response, feedback, power considerations, and lab practice.',
  $electzzjs${"slug": "electronics", "title": "Electronics", "description": "Electronics teaches how semiconductor devices become useful analog circuits. The syllabus links device physics to circuit models, biasing, small-signal analysis, amplifiers, op-amps, frequency response, feedback, power considerations, and lab practice.", "topics": [{"id": "9f714f0a-39e2-4732-9e75-b77a8c2d2abd", "type": "topic", "title": "Diodes and nonlinear circuits", "description": "This module establishes diodes and nonlinear circuits as the course's first working framework. It supplies the language and representations needed before the path advances to mosfet fundamentals.", "children": [{"id": "c23e9a03-c777-4eb6-94f0-c0904a001e3f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "I–V models", "children": [], "description": "I–V models gives diodes and nonlinear circuits a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. It appears before load lines because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "505f2fc3-a74f-46d5-b18d-c417e8fd9a56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Load lines", "children": [], "description": "Load lines identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within diodes and nonlinear circuits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After i–v models, load lines supplies what is needed to address rectifiers."}, {"id": "3bde3d02-7cd9-4cb3-b733-dfdbbdeffde9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rectifiers", "children": [], "description": "Rectifiers identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within diodes and nonlinear circuits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After load lines, rectifiers supplies what is needed to address clamps."}, {"id": "de9e745c-27f9-43a3-9e1e-63b32d0a01de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clamps", "children": [], "description": "Clamps identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within diodes and nonlinear circuits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After rectifiers, clamps supplies what is needed to address regulation."}, {"id": "33717c83-6579-4f44-a4b6-9b65b322e6de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regulation", "children": [], "description": "Regulation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within diodes and nonlinear circuits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, regulation carries the completed idea into mosfet fundamentals."}]}, {"id": "d93a675e-e55e-4e0a-a0e9-01dfa3e34ded", "type": "topic", "title": "MOSFET fundamentals", "description": "This module builds directly on diodes and nonlinear circuits and develops mosfet fundamentals. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for bjt fundamentals.", "children": [{"id": "70dedca2-021b-499b-80e8-3d39b18952d7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regions", "children": [], "description": "Regions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mosfet fundamentals. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before bias because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "0a7ffd14-776f-4233-a4ba-ae8635221f05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bias", "children": [], "description": "Bias identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mosfet fundamentals. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After regions, bias supplies what is needed to address transconductance."}, {"id": "2ba88933-543f-4e26-81ad-64a149405480", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transconductance", "children": [], "description": "Transconductance identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mosfet fundamentals. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After bias, transconductance supplies what is needed to address small-signal model."}, {"id": "02dc2ab3-43b3-41e3-a8c1-b1b45c4fb815", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Small-signal model", "children": [], "description": "Small-signal model gives mosfet fundamentals a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, small-signal model carries the completed idea into bjt fundamentals."}]}, {"id": "42559d80-f37e-46a6-a48c-88618ff5ad26", "type": "topic", "title": "BJT fundamentals", "description": "This module builds directly on mosfet fundamentals and develops bjt fundamentals. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for single-stage amplifiers.", "children": [{"id": "022f078c-4f1c-44c6-a317-7b9578a8aa7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Operating regions", "children": [], "description": "Operating regions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within bjt fundamentals. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before bias because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "04f2a1d6-db58-45f1-9cdd-e21aceca76f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bias", "children": [], "description": "Bias identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within bjt fundamentals. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After operating regions, bias supplies what is needed to address hybrid-pi model."}, {"id": "46f9aed5-28bc-41a8-b5bc-a2e40fabbe8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hybrid-pi model", "children": [], "description": "Hybrid-pi model gives bjt fundamentals a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. After bias, hybrid-pi model supplies what is needed to address thermal considerations."}, {"id": "a6ac2dfe-e944-4b2c-8244-c20b71542680", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Thermal considerations", "children": [], "description": "Thermal considerations identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within bjt fundamentals. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, thermal considerations carries the completed idea into single-stage amplifiers."}]}, {"id": "451affae-148c-4f4b-b7fb-ab10564cc6a3", "type": "topic", "title": "Single-stage amplifiers", "description": "This module builds directly on bjt fundamentals and develops single-stage amplifiers. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for frequency response.", "children": [{"id": "4342ed1d-6416-44be-9813-cc77494c6dee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common source/emitter", "children": [], "description": "Common source/emitter identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within single-stage amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before gain because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "d3d1ab4d-d649-41cb-8230-8160c754ab97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gain", "children": [], "description": "Gain identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within single-stage amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After common source/emitter, gain supplies what is needed to address input/output resistance."}, {"id": "437a9165-d70d-413a-8250-1c9df8eb18d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Input/output resistance", "children": [], "description": "Input/output resistance identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within single-stage amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, input/output resistance carries the completed idea into frequency response."}]}, {"id": "3cade1da-c63e-48be-8b2b-f8e987967317", "type": "topic", "title": "Frequency response", "description": "This module builds directly on single-stage amplifiers and develops frequency response. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for differential amplifiers.", "children": [{"id": "8cb01c7b-26cb-4007-b0d5-27742abe3108", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coupling/bypass capacitors", "children": [], "description": "Coupling/bypass capacitors identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within frequency response. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before miller effect because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "766e1634-b279-4285-9463-fe2858d8ac6e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Miller effect", "children": [], "description": "Miller effect identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within frequency response. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After coupling/bypass capacitors, miller effect supplies what is needed to address poles and zeros."}, {"id": "6abdaf56-36f2-4333-be5c-4748b38ec415", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poles and zeros", "children": [], "description": "Poles and zeros identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within frequency response. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, poles and zeros carries the completed idea into differential amplifiers."}]}, {"id": "bb706332-8264-4be6-866f-398d778c9bea", "type": "topic", "title": "Differential amplifiers", "description": "This module builds directly on frequency response and develops differential amplifiers. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for operational amplifiers.", "children": [{"id": "73c62f9f-1c57-44dc-bc04-12b46deb28cd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common mode", "children": [], "description": "Common mode identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within differential amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before cmrr because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "47028249-8543-462c-9563-af52acea636f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "CMRR", "children": [], "description": "CMRR identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within differential amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After common mode, cmrr supplies what is needed to address current mirrors."}, {"id": "f92bbca0-ad9f-4705-9aba-1f284eb5fb8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Current mirrors", "children": [], "description": "Current mirrors identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within differential amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After cmrr, current mirrors supplies what is needed to address active loads."}, {"id": "e1cb72ea-63b0-4eb5-a733-00a94f07ed71", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Active loads", "children": [], "description": "Active loads identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within differential amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, active loads carries the completed idea into operational amplifiers."}]}, {"id": "ecc60e3e-7926-4632-9175-a0cc2b5a02a1", "type": "topic", "title": "Operational amplifiers", "description": "This module builds directly on differential amplifiers and develops operational amplifiers. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for feedback.", "children": [{"id": "9434b76a-cf31-4b43-9dc5-27ed59f5db12", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ideal/nonideal behavior", "children": [], "description": "Ideal/nonideal behavior identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within operational amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before linear applications because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "f5d25286-dd60-43dc-bd76-acbdf7201b34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Linear applications", "children": [], "description": "Linear applications identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within operational amplifiers. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After ideal/nonideal behavior, linear applications supplies what is needed to address limitations."}, {"id": "59d8c354-b609-479f-b7a3-a7c7db776b8d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Limitations", "children": [], "description": "Limitations makes the validity limits of operational amplifiers explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. As the final topic in this module, limitations carries the completed idea into feedback."}]}, {"id": "62d5c555-2401-4b0c-a840-71ad14b79a69", "type": "topic", "title": "Feedback", "description": "This module builds directly on operational amplifiers and develops feedback. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for output stages.", "children": [{"id": "dde4f53a-54e0-4afa-9a5e-d9939da2c3b0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Loop gain", "children": [], "description": "Loop gain identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within feedback. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before gain desensitization because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "0c184112-cfb8-4353-b324-0a7257829fe4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gain desensitization", "children": [], "description": "Gain desensitization identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within feedback. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After loop gain, gain desensitization supplies what is needed to address impedance effects."}, {"id": "2927a9f7-621d-4d6a-85d2-3e1d1a67cadb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Impedance effects", "children": [], "description": "Impedance effects identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within feedback. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After gain desensitization, impedance effects supplies what is needed to address stability margins."}, {"id": "cb3c4fb5-390e-46cd-b0ae-1ebccd710abb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stability margins", "children": [], "description": "Stability margins makes the validity limits of feedback explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. As the final topic in this module, stability margins carries the completed idea into output stages."}]}, {"id": "94603410-fe69-4097-b47d-8a94a593830c", "type": "topic", "title": "Output stages", "description": "This module builds directly on feedback and develops output stages. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for oscillators and waveform generation.", "children": [{"id": "7c83c1bb-db8a-4393-a773-573fc6c91970", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Class A/B/AB", "children": [], "description": "Class A/B/AB identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within output stages. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before efficiency because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "db7e84ed-9a3d-4816-bb1b-1e6c45f0caa1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Efficiency", "children": [], "description": "Efficiency identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within output stages. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After class a/b/ab, efficiency supplies what is needed to address crossover."}, {"id": "8fdf217d-65c1-441e-9e40-942fa7504dba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crossover", "children": [], "description": "Crossover identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within output stages. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After efficiency, crossover supplies what is needed to address thermal design."}, {"id": "b1069fb0-199c-4565-825e-d2725483f653", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Thermal design", "children": [], "description": "Thermal design turns the theory of output stages into a defensible decision and exposes the relevant structure, cost, or performance trade-offs. As the final topic in this module, thermal design carries the completed idea into oscillators and waveform generation."}]}, {"id": "838d23a9-7919-46cb-a5ea-2f333803db78", "type": "topic", "title": "Oscillators and waveform generation", "description": "This module builds directly on output stages and develops oscillators and waveform generation. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for power electronics foundations.", "children": [{"id": "6331012e-5fe7-48d9-8f53-f291910a93ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Barkhausen criterion", "children": [], "description": "Barkhausen criterion identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within oscillators and waveform generation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before rc/lc because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "9259290a-3ccf-4c51-be98-e83a3b4eaa39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "RC/LC", "children": [], "description": "RC/LC identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within oscillators and waveform generation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After barkhausen criterion, rc/lc supplies what is needed to address comparators."}, {"id": "911d6261-d5ac-4ca4-9c70-34d3700eb92b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparators", "children": [], "description": "Comparators identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within oscillators and waveform generation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After rc/lc, comparators supplies what is needed to address timers."}, {"id": "65bd0b65-32c9-4ec9-8de6-6c72415299d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Timers", "children": [], "description": "Timers identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within oscillators and waveform generation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, timers carries the completed idea into power electronics foundations."}]}, {"id": "b69a1238-9880-4857-8c3a-e9665f6cc8f9", "type": "topic", "title": "Power electronics foundations", "description": "This module builds directly on oscillators and waveform generation and develops power electronics foundations. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for mixed-signal integration.", "children": [{"id": "da91603d-dd1d-46da-8f16-a856c377148e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Switching devices", "children": [], "description": "Switching devices identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within power electronics foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before converters because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "898363c5-601f-4bbc-9659-7128b4ea6b5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Converters", "children": [], "description": "Converters identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within power electronics foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After switching devices, converters supplies what is needed to address losses."}, {"id": "0c68618d-346f-42ba-9cbb-c3e8920ace52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Losses", "children": [], "description": "Losses identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within power electronics foundations. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After converters, losses supplies what is needed to address protection."}, {"id": "86aef6c6-ce7c-4f10-9ba1-1ff2be035c60", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Protection", "children": [], "description": "Protection explains how power electronics foundations behaves under misuse, faults, or constraints, which is essential for responsible real-world application. As the final topic in this module, protection carries the completed idea into mixed-signal integration."}]}, {"id": "7aeb2af2-d9ba-4cfe-b145-7e945c2e201e", "type": "topic", "title": "Mixed-signal integration", "description": "This culminating module draws on power electronics foundations and develops mixed-signal integration. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "73951d79-c27c-411b-9f0c-de5e2517c6ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ADC/DAC interfaces", "children": [], "description": "ADC/DAC interfaces identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mixed-signal integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before sensors because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "bc47eee1-6cd8-49ca-9e82-12046291a0b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensors", "children": [], "description": "Sensors identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mixed-signal integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After adc/dac interfaces, sensors supplies what is needed to address noise."}, {"id": "b5d086d2-db5e-461f-ac65-bada6c00d99c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Noise", "children": [], "description": "Noise identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mixed-signal integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After sensors, noise supplies what is needed to address grounding."}, {"id": "78e3147c-6ffc-4d49-baa4-5586d7df8f34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grounding", "children": [], "description": "Grounding identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within mixed-signal integration. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After noise, grounding supplies what is needed to address pcb-aware design."}, {"id": "973ba449-2ee5-4e87-adc2-2f3f8301c46f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "PCB-aware design", "children": [], "description": "PCB-aware design turns the theory of mixed-signal integration into a defensible decision and exposes the relevant structure, cost, or performance trade-offs. As the final course topic, pcb-aware design requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$electzzjs$::jsonb,
